2026-07-06 12:51:39,156 [DEBUG] anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'headers': {'anthropic-user-profile-id': <anthropic.Omit object at 0x7f47387018b0>}, 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f6f2804c-9b98-47c9-8c62-b0e8edd087ba', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Extract all job/position listings from this career page HTML.\nReturn a JSON array where each element has:\n- "title": job title string\n- "url": full URL to the job posting (resolve relative URLs against https://thefuturesociety.org/work-with-us/)\n- "location": location if mentioned, else null\n- "role_type": "Full-time", "Part-time", "Fellowship", "Internship", or null\n\nOnly include actual job openings, internships, and fellowships.\nIgnore navigation links, news articles, blog posts, event listings, etc.\nIf there are no job listings on the page, return an empty array: []\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no other text.\n\n---\n\n<div class="fl-page-content" id="fl-main-content" itemprop="mainContentOfPage" role="main"><div class="fl-content-full container"><div class="row"><div class="fl-content col-md-12"><article class="fl-post post-5588 page type-page status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry" id="fl-post-5588" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/CreativeWork"><div class="fl-post-content clearfix" itemprop="text"><div class="fl-builder-content fl-builder-content-5588 fl-builder-content-primary fl-builder-global-templates-locked" data-post-id="5588"><div class="fl-row fl-row-full-width fl-row-bg-none fl-node-s2ghmj54kvet fl-row-default-height fl-row-align-center" data-node="s2ghmj54kvet"><div class="fl-row-content-wrap"><div class="uabb-row-separator uabb-top-row-separator"></div><div class="fl-row-content fl-row-fixed-width fl-node-content"><div class="fl-col-group fl-node-djfx3kivaoup" data-node="djfx3kivaoup"><div class="fl-col fl-node-gphlq7u2rota fl-col-bg-color" data-node="gphlq7u2rota"><div class="fl-col-content fl-node-content"><div class="fl-module fl-module-pp-heading fl-node-oi0te18jnsyf" data-node="oi0te18jnsyf"><div class="fl-module-content fl-node-content"><div class="pp-heading-content"><div class="pp-heading pp-left"><h2 class="heading-title"> <span class="title-text pp-primary-title">Current openings</span></h2></div></div></div></div><div class="fl-module fl-module-rich-text fl-node-skyul0973gjh" data-node="skyul0973gjh"><div class="fl-module-content fl-node-content"><div class="fl-rich-text"><p><strong>Please note</strong>:To apply for a role, please use the application form linked in the job posting. For questions about open positions or the application process, contact <b></b> <a href="mailto:info@thefuturesociety.org">jobs@thefuturesociety.org</a>.</p></div></div></div><div class="fl-module fl-module-pp-content-grid fl-node-vlzocrwgjt2m job-listings" data-node="vlzocrwgjt2m"><div class="fl-module-content fl-node-content"><div class="pp-posts-wrapper"><div class="pp-content-posts" style="--items-count: 1;--column-xl: 1;--column-lg: 1;--column-md: 1;--column-sm: 1;"><div class="pp-content-post-grid pp-masonry-active clearfix" data-loading-animation="fade" data-loop-count="1" data-paged="0" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Collection"><div class="pp-content-post pp-content-grid-post pp-grid-custom post-10777 job type-job status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry job_location-remote time_requirement-full-time" data-id="10777" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/CreativeWork"><meta content="Communications Coordinator" itemid="https://thefuturesociety.org/job/communications-coordinator/" itemprop="mainEntityOfPage" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/WebPage"/><meta content="2026-06-22T13:06:32+00:00" itemprop="datePublished"/><meta content="2026-06-23T15:53:28+00:00" itemprop="dateModified"/><div itemprop="publisher" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/Organization"><meta content="The Future Society" itemprop="name"/><div itemprop="logo" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/ImageObject"><meta content="https://thefuturesociety.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/tfs_logoPNG.png" itemprop="url"/></div></div><div itemprop="author" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person"><meta content="https://thefuturesociety.org/author/eloise/" itemprop="url"/><meta content="Eloise Dunn" itemprop="name"/></div><div itemprop="image" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/ImageObject"><meta content="https://thefuturesociety.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Operations-and-Project-Analyst-Graphic-1.png" itemprop="url"/><meta content="1200" itemprop="width"/><meta content="500" itemprop="height"/></div><div itemprop="interactionStatistic" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/InteractionCounter"><meta content="https://schema.org/CommentAction" itemprop="interactionType"/><meta content="0" itemprop="userInteractionCount"/></div><div class="job-listing-wrapper"><div class="job-listing-top"><div class="job-listing-title"><h3>Communications Coordinator</h3></div><div class="job-listing-button"><a href="#">Explore Role</a></div></div><div class="job-listing-bottom"><div class="job-location"><i class="fa-sharp fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i>Remote</div><div class="job-time-requirement"><i class="fa-solid fa-clock"></i>Full-Time</div></div><div class="job-listing-hidden-content-wrapper"><div class="job-listing-hidden-content"><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Position: </strong><strong>Communications Coordinator</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Application Deadline:</strong> Applications will be processed on a rolling basis – we review applications as we receive them. We expect that we will stop accepting applications after three weeks, but we may close the round sooner if we receive a high volume of applications. Candidates are strongly encouraged to apply early.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Employment Status:</strong> Full-time, fixed-term employee position (12 months, with possibility of extension or conversion to permanent depending on organizational needs and funding)</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote, based between Eastern Time (ET) and Central European Time (CET). Applicants must have the legal right to live and work in the country where they are based. Please note that TFS is currently unable to sponsor visas.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Starting Date:</strong> As soon as possible after offer, estimated start in August 2026</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Compensation:</strong> \xa0The Future Society (TFS) uses a transparent, formula-based compensation framework that takes into account role level and geographic location to promote fairness, consistency, and equity across our global team. Compensation is not negotiated on an individual basis. The compensation for this role for candidates based outside the U.S. is between $58,400 and $75,300. For U.S.-based candidates, the compensation is between $74,400 and $92,100. (with further adjustments for specific locations with a higher cost of living).</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Benefits:</strong> For a U.S.-based hire, benefits include medical, dental, and vision insurance as well as a 403(b) retirement plan with an employer match at three percent of salary, 30 days of annual leave (including floating public holidays), and 10 days of sick leave each year. For non-U.S. employees, we match the U.S. standard as closely as possible or use local mandatory levels, whichever is highest.</p><p class="has-background wp-block-paragraph" style="background-color:#e6e2fc"><strong>How to apply:</strong> Please complete a <a href="https://tally.so/r/wQAl48?RoleTitle=Communications%20Coordinator&amp;RoleRowID=57&amp;ReqTimeZone=Are%20you%20able%20to%20work%20from%20%20a%20location%20between%20UTC%20-5%20and%20UTC%202%3F&amp;Q1=Question%201%3A%20What%20makes%20you%20a%20good%20fit%20for%20this%20role%20and%20for%20The%20Future%20Society%3F%20Be%20as%20specific%20as%20you%20can.%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q2=Question%202%3A%20Tell%20us%20about%20a%20piece%20of%20content%20that%20communicated%20a%20complex%20idea%20well.%20What%20made%20it%20effective%3F%20The%20content%20could%20have%20been%20created%20by%20you%20or%20someone%20else.%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q3=Question%203%3A%20Give%20an%20example%20of%20a%20process%20that%20you%20proactively%20improved%20in%20a%20work%20setting.%20What%20was%20the%20problem%2C%20what%20steps%20did%20you%20take%2C%20and%20what%20was%20the%20outcome%3F%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q4=Please%20share%20links%20to%20your%20best%20pieces%20of%20written%20work%20(up%20to%20three%20examples).%20These%20can%20be%20articles%2C%20blog%20posts%2C%20research%20summaries%2C%20newsletters%2C%20or%20similar." rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">job application form</a> for this position. Any questions about the application process should be sent to <a href="mailto:jobs@thefuturesociety.org" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">jobs@thefuturesociety.org</a>. Note: Applications will not be accepted via email, please use the form.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Position Summary:</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Communications is an important part of The Future Society’s mission to align AI through better governance. By making complex policy ideas accessible and amplifying the work of our experts and partners, we help inform public debate and support better AI governance outcomes.</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Future Society (TFS) is looking for an organized and proactive Communications Coordinator to support and help grow our communication function, ensuring that our research, policy engagement, fundraising, and organizational initiatives are communicated clearly, consistently, and effectively across digital and external channels.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The role will initially report to the Operations Manager, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eloisedunn/" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Eloise Dunn</a>, while working closely with the COO, policy teams, and senior leadership. This hire will play a key role in amplifying the important AI governance work we do. The successful candidate will be a skilled, hands-on communicator who is passionate about TFS’s mission of aligning AI through better governance, and they will be proactive, autonomous, and versatile.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">While this is a fixed-term position for now, this is an exciting opportunity to join TFS at a pivotal moment as we invest in and expand our communications function. Over the next 12 months, we aim to strengthen how we communicate our research, policy engagement, events, and organizational impact to a growing international audience. This role will play an important part in building the systems, processes, and outputs that support that growth, with opportunities for the position and the wider communications function to evolve over time.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Why join The Future Society?</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>A chance to do meaningful work for a mission-driven, independent 501(c)(3) nonprofit with a track record of outsized impact.</li><li>Meaningful work at the frontier of AI governance. TFS has a track record of translating policy research into real governance outcomes, and this role is central to how that work reaches the world.</li><li>You’ll be building something. The communications function is growing, and the person in this role will help establish its systems, rhythms, and outputs over the next 12 months, with room for the role to evolve as the function does.</li><li>You’ll be joining a small, high-performing global team connected to an international network of AI policy experts, governments, academic institutions, and civil society organizations.</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Essential Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Draft, format, and publish blog posts, reports, and other publications on the <a href="https://thefuturesociety.org/">TFS website</a> (WordPress) in collaboration with AI Governance teams.</li><li>Own communications workflows for publications and campaigns, coordinating timelines across researchers, leadership, and external partners.</li><li>Format reports, slide decks, and other documents using existing TFS templates and brand guidelines, primarily using Canva.</li><li>Plan, create, and publish social media content using the content calendar system, ensuring posts accurately reflect the content of publications and are tailored to each platform.</li><li>Support communications for major TFS convenings, including <a href="https://www.aiathens.org/">The Athens Roundtable</a> and other high-profile events, conferences, and public appearances by TFS staff.</li><li>Provide logistical and communications support for our annual flagship event The Athens Roundtable, such as speaker communications, digital assets, event promotion and post-event publishing</li><li>Manage the newsletter production cycle: content aggregation, formatting, scheduling and distribution</li><li>Manage website content and coordinate with external developers to maintain and improve TFS’s digital presence.</li><li>Monitor communications metrics (social media engagement, newsletter open rates, website traffic), and produce regular performance reports and recommend improvements based on communications data.</li><li>Support the production and assembly of organizational fundraising and development communications, including one-pagers, donor briefing packs, impact reports and narratives, grant collateral, annual report content and stewardship materials) under the direction of the COO.</li><li>Support internal communications around major organizational announcements.</li><li>Explore and responsibly use AI-enabled communications tools to improve efficiency and effectiveness.</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>2+ years of experience in communications, editorial, or digital publishing.</li><li>Commitment to TFS’s mission of aligning AI through better governance. Previous experience working in AI governance is not required for this role, but a genuine interest in AI governance, AI safety, or technology policy is important. You do not need a technical background, but you must be able to read and understand policy-oriented material on these topics in order to write accurate summaries and social media content.</li><li>Self-directed and reliable, with strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple concurrent tasks and deadlines independently.</li><li>Detail-oriented, diligent, and tenacious, consistently completing tasks to a high standard.</li><li>Excellent written English, including the ability to write clearly and concisely for different formats (social media, newsletters, website) and to proofread and edit others’ work.</li><li>Experience working with social media platforms (LinkedIn and X/Twitter) in a professional context.</li><li>Excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate with diverse stakeholders.</li><li>Proficiency in CMS platforms, email marketing tools, and social media management.</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Preferred</em></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Proficiency with WordPress, Mailchimp, and Canva</li><li>Familiarity working with and interpreting analytics (e.g., Google Analytics, social media analytics)</li><li>Experience in a small company or organization.</li><li>Experience operating in a global and/or remote-first work environment. Familiarity working in both the U.S. and Europe is helpful.</li><li>Experience in a non-profit, think tank, policy, or research organization, especially in the AI Governance field.</li><li>Willingness and ability to travel both domestically and internationally for work, including for team retreats</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The ideal candidate for this role will have a lot of the skills and experiences described above. However, you may not need to tick every box to be a great candidate. If you are hesitant about applying because you’re not sure if you’re the perfect fit, we encourage you to apply.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>About The Future Society:</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://thefuturesociety.org/">The Future Society</a> (TFS) is an independent 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization operating in the United States and Europe with the mission to align AI through better governance. We develop, advocate for, and facilitate the implementation of governance mechanisms designed to ensure AI systems are safe and uphold fundamental values. Through our work, we collaborate with intergovernmental organizations, governments, companies, academic institutions, think tanks, and other civil society organizations. You can learn more about our work on our<a href="https://thefuturesociety.org/about-us/"> About Us page.</a></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">We are a small, high-performing, and mission-driven team operating globally with a collaborative culture that values integrity, curiosity, and collective problem-solving.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">We operate primarily remotely. In order to overlap with the whole team, team members need to be available for calls between 4pm and 6pm UTC.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Evaluation Process:</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Stage 1: Application</li><li>Stage 2: Work Test</li><li>Stage 3: First Interview</li><li>Stage 4: Second Interview</li><li>Stage 5: Reference Checks &amp; Employment Offer</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>TFS is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, national origin, political affiliation, sexual orientation, marital status, disability, age, membership in an employee organization, parental status, military service, or other non-merit factors.</em></p><div class="wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-fe48e5de wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link has-text-align-center wp-element-button" href="https://tally.so/r/wQAl48?RoleTitle=Communications%20Coordinator&amp;RoleRowID=57&amp;ReqTimeZone=Are%20you%20able%20to%20work%20from%20%20a%20location%20between%20UTC%20-5%20and%20UTC%202%3F&amp;Q1=Question%201%3A%20What%20makes%20you%20a%20good%20fit%20for%20this%20role%20and%20for%20The%20Future%20Society%3F%20Be%20as%20specific%20as%20you%20can.%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q2=Question%202%3A%20Tell%20us%20about%20a%20piece%20of%20content%20that%20communicated%20a%20complex%20idea%20well.%20What%20made%20it%20effective%3F%20The%20content%20could%20have%20been%20created%20by%20you%20or%20someone%20else.%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q3=Question%203%3A%20Give%20an%20example%20of%20a%20process%20that%20you%20proactively%20improved%20in%20a%20work%20setting.%20What%20was%20the%20problem%2C%20what%20steps%20did%20you%20take%2C%20and%20what%20was%20the%20outcome%3F%20%5Bsuggested%20limit%3A%20200%20words%5D&amp;Q4=Please%20share%20links%20to%20your%20best%20pieces%20of%20written%20work%20(up%20to%20three%20examples).%20These%20can%20be%20articles%2C%20blog%20posts%2C%20research%20summaries%2C%20newsletters%2C%20or%20similar." rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Click to Apply</a></div></div><p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p></div></div></div></div><div class="pp-grid-space"></div></div><div class="fl-clear"></div></div><!-- .pp-content-posts --></div></div></div><div class="fl-module fl-module-rich-text fl-node-62mtdvfy4kxo" data-node="62mtdvfy4kxo"><div class="fl-module-content fl-node-content"><div class="fl-rich-text"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="uabb-js-breakpoint" style="display: none;"></div></div><!-- .fl-post-content --></article><div class="fl-comments"></div> <!-- .fl-post --></div></div></div></div>'}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5'}}
